            "of significant digits. For example when we want to convert mm to inch (1 mm = 0.0393701 inch), then by multiplying 67.5 mm to inch will give us 2.65748175 inches we have to round off the number",
            "4. ZEROS to the right of the significant figure to proper significant digits.",
            "Page",
