            "Dynamics",
            "You know from unit 2: Kinematics that when an object is dropped, it accelerates toward the center of Earth. Newton's second law states that a net force on an object is responsible for its acceleration. If air resistance is negligible, the net force on a falling object is the gravitational force, commonly called its weight w. Since weight is a force as have the same units as force newton (N). Weight can be denoted as a vector w because it has a direction..",
            "Consider an object with mass 'm' falling downward towards Earth. It experiences only the downward force of gravity, which has magnitude",
