        "solution": "In Standard form / scientific notation we can write the term as\n\nBondlength = 0.000000000074 × 10⁰ m\n\nFor Standard form / scientific notation in order to get mantissa (M) in which the 1st digit before the decimal is non-zero, we have to move the decimal 11 digits to the right. Therefore, the power of 10 will be negative 11, that is\n\nBondlength = 7.4 × 10⁻¹¹ m\n\nAnswer\n\nWhich is the bond length for diatomic hydrogen in standard form / scientific notation.",
