            "text": "Equilibrium is stable as long as the vertical line from the centre of mass remains inside the area of the base of the body. If a disruption moves the vertical line from the centre of mass outside of the base, then the equilibrium is unstable. Neutral equilibrium exists when any disruptive force acts horizontally but the vertical height of the centre of mass remains unchanged. Taller people are generally less stable than shorter people because their higher centre of mass can be more easily pushed outside base of the structure, sometimes called the footprint. Some toys are more stable, then they look as they right by themselves if they are disturbed.",
