            "text": "The scientific definition of work differs in some ways from its everyday meaning. Certain things we think of as hard work, such as writing an exam or carrying a heavy load on level ground, are not work as defined by a scientist. For work, in the scientific sense, to be done, a force must be exerted and there must be motion or displacement in the direction of the force.",
