            "text": "In order to construct a thermometer, we make use of a certain physical property of matter that increases or decreases uniformly with rise and fall in temperature. This particular property of a substance that increases and decreases uniformly with temperature and can be used for the measurement of temperature is called thermometric property. Some examples of thermometric properties include the volume of a liquid, length of a solid, gas pressure, electrical resistance and electromotive force.",
