            "text": "It is also possible for a substance to change directly from a solid to a gas. This process is called sublimation. For example, sublimation occurs when dry ice, which is solid (frozen) carbon dioxide, changes directly to gaseous carbon dioxide without passing through the liquid state. Figure 8.12 (a)",
