            "text": "property of damaging the ozone layer. Modern refrigerators usually use a refrigerant called hydrofluorocarbon (HFC), which was supposed to have zero potential to deplete the ozone layer. However in 1974 researchers predicted that emissions of HFCs could damage Earth's atmosphere by the catalytic destruction of ozone in the stratosphere. The hypothesis has been proven in 1985 by measurements which have shown the destruction of the ozone layer over Antarctica. Scientists are now looking to develop new refrigerant that is natural and have low global warming potential (GWP) and zero Ozone Depletion Potential (ODP).",
