          "ans": "Conduction: flow of heat through matter from hot to cold parts without bulk movement. Hotter atoms vibrate more and pass energy to neighbours by collisions; in metals free electrons gain energy and diffuse to colder parts. Applications: metal cooking pots, wire gauze over a flame, pot holders/table mats of poor conductors, woolen clothes, igloos, ice box with cork, soldering (p.234-238).",
