          "ans": "Thermal conductivity measures a substance’s ability to conduct heat. The rate of heat flow Q/t through a slab increases with temperature difference (T_h − T_c) and area A, decreases with thickness L, and depends on the material: Q/t = k A (T_h − T_c)/L, so k = QL/(A t (T_h − T_c)); unit W m⁻¹ K⁻¹ (p.238-239).",
